+# Morris Fleet Vigilance — Setup Checklist
+## Post-Merge Deploy + Re-Enqueue Sweep (Check 17 / STORY-800)
+
+This file documents the configuration required to run `post-merge-sweep.py` in production.
+
+## Required Environment Variables
+
+| Variable | Required | Default | Description |
+|----------|----------|---------|-------------|
+| `OPS_CONSOLE_API_KEY` | **YES** | _(none)_ | API key for `GET /api/dispatch/history` + cancel/re-enqueue POSTs. Script raises `ValueError` if unset or empty. |
+| `OPS_CONSOLE_BASE_URL` | No | `http://localhost:8005` | Base URL of the ops-console API. |
+| `MARK_TEAMS_CHAT_ID` | Yes (for DM) | _(none)_ | Teams chat ID for Mark's 1:1 DM (used by `send_teams_dm()`). |
+| `MORRIS_GRAPH_TOKEN` | Yes (for DM) | _(none)_ | Bearer token for Microsoft Graph API (`POST /me/chats/{id}/messages`). |
+| `FLEET_SWEEP_LOOKBACK_HOURS` | No | `24` | Query window for eligible failed dispatch_items. Increase to `48` if deploying infrequently. |
+| `TECH_DEV_AGENTS_REPO` | No | `/home/hermes/workspace/tech-dev-agents` | Path to the tech-dev-agents git repository on the Morris VM. |
+| `FLEET_SWEEP_STATE_FILE` | No | `/home/hermes/state/morris/last-fleet-vigilance-merge-sweep.txt` | Path to the sweep state file (SHA + timestamp of last processed merge). |
+| `FLEET_HEALTH_FILE` | No | `/home/hermes/state/morris/fleet-health.md` | Path to the fleet-health audit log. |
+
+## State File
+
+**Path:** `/home/hermes/state/morris/last-fleet-vigilance-merge-sweep.txt`
+
+**Format:**
+```
+<40-char git SHA>
+<ISO-8601 UTC timestamp e.g. 2026-04-30T12:00:00Z>
+```
+
+**Permissions:** 644, owned by `hermes`.
+
+**Bootstrap (first run):** On first invocation, if the state file does not exist, the script
+auto-initializes it from `git rev-parse HEAD` and exits with no deploys or re-enqueues. No manual
+seeding required.
+
+**Reset:** Delete the state file to force the next run to bootstrap from HEAD again.
+
+## Kill Switch
+
+To disable Check 17 without deleting the script:
+
+```bash
+# Option A: remove the invocation from SKILL.md (preferred)
+# Option B: make the script non-executable
+chmod -x /home/hermes/dev/tech-dev-agents/deployment/morris/scripts/post-merge-sweep.py
+```
+
+## Audit Trail
+
+Every sweep cycle appends a `[POST-MERGE-SWEEP]` line to `fleet-health.md`:
+
+```
+[POST-MERGE-SWEEP] sha=14b771b9 deploy=success reenqueue=11 eligible=11
+[POST-MERGE-SWEEP] sha=deadbeef deploy=FAILED smoke_ok=False — CRIT escalated to Mark
+[POST-MERGE-SWEEP] no new merges — no-op
+```
+
+Loki picks up `[POST-MERGE-SWEEP]` lines from the fleet-health log for alerting.
+
+## Deployment
+
+The script ships with the Morris codebase at:
+`deployment/morris/scripts/post-merge-sweep.py`
+
+Deploy via the standard push-code.sh mechanism:
+```bash
+./deployment/vm/push-code.sh all
+```
+
+After deployment, run once manually to bootstrap the state file:
+```bash
+OPS_CONSOLE_API_KEY=<key> python3 deployment/morris/scripts/post-merge-sweep.py
+```
